WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.860
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:07.470
Today I want to talk about habits,
habits of a lazy language learner.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.130
Remember if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe, click

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.840
on the bell for notifications.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.490
Yeah, I want to talk about my
language learning style now.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:21.720
Uh, and what I would call being a
lazy language learner, which doesn't

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.720
necessarily mean that you aren't
being a successful language learner.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.110
It just means that you're being
lazy the way I'm being lazy.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.100
And so there are seven habits I think
that we need to acquire if we're going to

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:39.360
be effective, successful, lazy language
learners, the first is to set low goals.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.750
Okay, so on my 90-Day Challenge, I've
set my goal for creating LingQs at

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.110
13 for Arabic and 13 for Persian.

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:52.870
And there was a time when I was
trying to do a hundred new LingQs

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.860
in Arabic, Persian, and Turkish.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.300
It was simply too much.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.699
Um, so I've changed my style.

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:00.989
Now I set low goals.

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:05.370
Now I regularly exceed these goals
if I look at my statistics, but

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.259
the low goal just gets me going.

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:11.325
I don't see, you know that I, I
don't feel any great burden or

00:01:11.325 --> 00:01:13.065
obligation I just get started.

00:01:13.065 --> 00:01:16.785
And once I'm launched, I'll
generally, you know, exceed my goals.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:19.905
But my first habit therefore,
is to set low goals.

00:01:19.935 --> 00:01:23.625
Now I have a bit of a cheat sheet here
and I'm going to make sure I don't forget.

00:01:24.135 --> 00:01:28.005
The second thing is don't
compete with others.

00:01:28.095 --> 00:01:30.015
I'm not competing with other people.

00:01:30.285 --> 00:01:34.395
Uh, in my challenge, I'm not
comparing myself to others.

00:01:34.425 --> 00:01:35.985
Some people are going faster.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.320
I see that I'm ranked 1,572 on my streak.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.310
That's fine.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.040
Uh, some people are going
to pronounce better.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.150
Some people are going to learn
faster, slower, whatever.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.520
It doesn't matter, I'm
learning it for myself.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:50.930
So I'm not competing.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.670
It reduces the stress level.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.360
Anything that reduces the stress
level makes learning more enjoyable,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.310
makes learning more effective.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.850
The next thing is to be a lazy
language you've got to go with the

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.979
flow, do things that you want to do.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:10.889
For example, uh, I'm on my Arabic and
Persian challenge, but lo and behold, my

00:02:10.889 --> 00:02:17.340
wife starts watching a Danish series on
Netflix and I love listening to Danish and

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.990
there's lots of words I don't understand.

00:02:19.484 --> 00:02:21.495
So I say, I'm going to do a bit of Danish.

00:02:21.495 --> 00:02:25.695
So I spent a day out of my week or
more listening to the mini stories

00:02:25.695 --> 00:02:29.625
in Danish, uh, Hans Christian
Anderson stories in Danish, uh,

00:02:29.655 --> 00:02:31.454
saving a bunch of Danish words.

00:02:31.454 --> 00:02:35.535
So that I have some sense of some
of these words that I hear in this,

00:02:35.535 --> 00:02:39.825
uh, TV series called The Sea View
Hotel that I don't understand.

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:41.235
And now I understand that a lot better.

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:46.055
Uh, similarly I started watching
an Egyptian movie for fun.

00:02:46.535 --> 00:02:48.450
So follow your wishes.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:53.460
And I guess that ties into the fourth
habit of a lazy language learning

00:02:53.609 --> 00:02:57.420
learner, and that is treat language
learning as a form of entertainment.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.640
Okay, and include entertainment.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.350
So obviously, when I watched the Danish
series, I understand a lot of it.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.899
And by doing a little work on LingQ,
I understand a lot more, uh, with the

00:03:09.929 --> 00:03:14.609
movies, the Egyptian movies, I'm speaking
with my tutor or aat least we're going

00:03:14.609 --> 00:03:18.299
over the mini stories in Egyptin Arabic,
which is different from standard Arabic.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:24.420
And my hope is that I'll understand
Egyptian movies better, but watching

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:29.870
an Egyptian movie, like the movie I
saw, I think it's called, uh, Asmaa uh,

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.520
about a woman who has AIDS in Egypt.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.210
I can enjoy the movie.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:35.640
I get the...

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:36.980
I hear the language.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.030
I don't really understand much of
it, but it's a form of entertainment.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:44.000
It brings me into the culture,
language learning is...

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.670
should be entertainment as well.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.490
It shouldn't just be routine and
drills and that kind of thing.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:53.160
So allow yourself to be entertained.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.710
Um, another thing about being a lazy
language learner is I don't prepare

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.390
for my sessions with my tutor.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.670
I don't prepare, I just show up, um, with
Mohammed and Egyptian Arabic, we just

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:08.280
open up a mini story, I read a bit of it.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.960
Then maybe we have some questions on it.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.810
Then we fade into a
discussion of something else.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:18.329
In Egyptian Arabic or in Standard Arabic
more, if we're free conversation, it's

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:20.190
more Standard Arabic than Egyptian Arabic.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:23.250
I struggle in both, but I don't prepare.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:27.570
I just show up and, and again,
whatever exposure I get, whatever

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:32.070
I'm doing with the language, engaging
with the language during that hour

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.170
with Mohammed is all to the good.

00:04:34.664 --> 00:04:40.424
So no need to get hung up about preparing
for the session, lazy language learner,

00:04:40.515 --> 00:04:43.965
you just show up one-on-one and benefit.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.205
Another important...

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:54.315
number six habit of a lazy language
learner is when you're tired of doing

00:04:54.554 --> 00:04:56.265
something, go and do something else.

00:04:56.455 --> 00:04:58.215
Introduce is a lot of variety.

00:04:59.375 --> 00:05:02.734
As long as you are engaging with the
language you are achieving something.

00:05:03.225 --> 00:05:05.925
So you're tired of listening,
go do more reading.

00:05:05.955 --> 00:05:09.585
I sometimes feel I have to push
myself a little bit on the reading

00:05:09.585 --> 00:05:13.215
because I think the reading is, is
essential to acquiring vocabulary.

00:05:13.635 --> 00:05:16.995
Uh, obviously the listening is easier
to do while I'm doing other chores,

00:05:17.535 --> 00:05:22.785
um, but uh, introduce movies and
switch from one language to another,

00:05:23.085 --> 00:05:26.325
uh, introduce variety around it.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:27.735
Keeps it interesting.

00:05:27.915 --> 00:05:30.975
You have less of a sense that
you're constantly sort of

00:05:31.395 --> 00:05:32.865
pounding on the same door.

00:05:33.015 --> 00:05:35.205
Variety keeps things interesting.

00:05:35.355 --> 00:05:40.355
Enables you to be a lazy language
or, and the final seventh habit

00:05:40.445 --> 00:05:46.625
of a lazy language learner is
in a way don't measure yourself.

00:05:47.495 --> 00:05:51.935
Don't compare yourself to what you did
before or where you would like to be,

00:05:51.935 --> 00:05:54.725
or what other people do don't measure.

00:05:55.025 --> 00:05:59.195
Accept the fact that
the process is success.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:04.034
Success is the fact that you are engaging
with the language, accept the fact

00:06:04.034 --> 00:06:09.125
that whatever you're doing as a lazy
language learner, it is helping you.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.474
It is helping the brain
get used to the language.

00:06:12.284 --> 00:06:14.145
Some days you would like to be better.

00:06:14.145 --> 00:06:17.235
Some days you're better
than you thought you were.

00:06:17.474 --> 00:06:20.745
Uh, sometimes you feel you have achieved
a lot over the last three months.

00:06:20.745 --> 00:06:22.724
Some days you feel you're treading water.

00:06:23.205 --> 00:06:24.104
It doesn't matter.

00:06:24.135 --> 00:06:29.729
The fact that you are engaging with
the language is in itself success.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.260
The fact that you are enjoying the
process, the fact that you are continuing

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:38.760
to get involved with the language,
listening, reading, watching movies,

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:43.710
speaking, whenever you're doing that
is that that makes you successful

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.090
because you're continuing to do it.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.370
And if you continue to do it, and if you
enjoy the process, even as a lazy language

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:57.284
learner, you will reach your goals faster
than, in my opinion, forcing yourself

00:06:57.344 --> 00:06:59.385
to do things that you don't want to do.

00:06:59.835 --> 00:07:05.474
So there you have the seven
habits of a lazy language learner,

00:07:05.505 --> 00:07:07.365
which I consider myself to be.

00:07:07.635 --> 00:07:10.125
Although I do spend a lot
of time with my languages.

00:07:10.395 --> 00:07:10.875
Bye for now.

